        "original_id": "f4381b51-35d3-5cf4-a465-139e3438b395",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Coll, Loch Breachacha, Scotland\n- Structures: Breachacha Castle, Breacachadh Castle, Dùn Dubh\n- Topics: sandy beaches, sand dunes, corncrakes, hillforts\n\nFacts:\n- Coll is an Inner Hebridean island in Scotland.\n- Coll is known for sandy beaches that rise into large sand dunes.\n- Coll is known for its corncrakes.\n- Coll is known for Breacachadh Castle.\n- Breachacha Castle, also spelled Breacachadh, refers to either of two structures on the shore of Loch Breachacha on Coll.\n- Dùn Dubh is a hillfort located on the island of Coll.",
